      "domain": "information-and-ideas",
      "skill": "inferences",
      "passage": "Acorn barnacles feed only while submerged, sweeping food from the water with feathery limbs; when the tide drops below them, they seal their shells and wait. On any one shore, barnacles of a single species settle at many heights on the rocks, and the water that washes over all of them carries the same food. Yet researchers measuring growth find a steady gradient: the higher on the rocks a barnacle lives, the more slowly it grows. Since the food supply is the same at every height, the gradient suggests that ______",
