      "passage": "An apple tree grown from seed is a gamble: the fruit it eventually bears may be small, sour, and nothing like the apple the seed came from. ______ a branch cut from a favorite tree and grafted onto young rootstock produces fruit identical to the parent's, which is why an orchard's named varieties are always propagated by grafting.",
