      "explanation": "**Choice D is correct.** The first sentence describes the unpredictable outcome of growing from seed; the second describes the guaranteed outcome of grafting. Two opposite outcomes call for a contrast word.\n\n**The Full Solution:**\n- Map what each sentence claims. Seeds: a gamble — the fruit may resemble the parent's not at all.\n- Grafting: certainty — fruit \"identical to the parent's.\"\n- Same goal (a new tree), opposite results (unpredictable versus identical): the second sentence is set against the first.\n- \"By contrast\" marks exactly that opposition.\n- How to spot it: when the topic stays the same but the outcome flips from one sentence to the next, the blank wants a contrast transition.\n\n**Why the other choices are wrong:**\n- A: \"In addition\" promises another point of the same kind, but the grafting sentence pushes the opposite way from the seed sentence.\n- B: \"As a result\" would make grafting's reliability a consequence of seeds being unreliable, and no such causal link exists.\n- C: \"For instance\" would offer grafting as an example of the seed gamble, when it is the alternative to it."
